          "id": "aat:300435416",
          "type": "Type",
          "_label": "descriptive note"
        }
      ],
      "content": "a woollen fabric 30 yards in length, originally made in a parish in Norfolk, north of Norwich (OEngl Wurdestede, later Wurthstede, Worthsted), made from well-twisted yarn spun of long-staple wool combed to lay the fibers parallel; single, half-double and double refer to the thickness of the cloth (OED s.v. worsted); also manufactured in St Omer (imported)"
    }
  ],
